+// liveStepMoleculeIdsShell (ga-i5bu7) fetches the set of molecule ids that
+// currently have a live (status=in_progress) step child. It populates the
+// $live_step_molecules shell variable ONCE per script; every "new work" tier
+// that follows reads that variable via poolDemandExcludeLiveMoleculeStepJQ
+// instead of re-querying bd, so a script with several tiers (e.g.
+// poolDemandCountShell's three) pays this cost once, not per tier.
+//
+// Deliberately a SEPARATE upfront bd call rather than a per-candidate lookup:
+// gastown.dog-1's original investigation (ga-i5bu7 comment, 2026-08-29)
+// proposed a per-candidate `bd list --parent <molecule_id> --status
+// in_progress` call and flagged it as the reason NOT to hand-roll the fix
+// solo — in the worst case (every candidate in a 20-row window is a
+// molecule-driven story) that's up to 20 extra bd subprocess spawns per
+// probe invocation, run continuously by every dog/wa-worker/ps-worker
+// citywide. One bd list --status in_progress --type step call up front,
+// reused by every tier, is bounded regardless of candidate count.
+//
+// quiet=true (worker-probe contexts: poolDemandFirstRowFunctionScript)
+// redirects stderr and defaults $live_step_molecules to "[]" on any
+// failure. This is a demand-DISCOVERY filter: failing open (treat nothing
+// as in-flight) merely reproduces today's ga-i5bu7 status quo rather than
+// something worse, whereas failing closed on a transient hiccup here would
+// read as "everything is in-flight" and hide ALL pool demand citywide —
+// a materially worse outage than the bug this fix closes.
+//
+// quiet=false (poolDemandCountShell) leaves bd's own exit status live and
+// contains no stderr redirection, matching that function's own no-masking
+// contract: a real bd failure must surface as an error, not be silently
+// read as "zero in-flight steps" (see poolDemandCountShell's doc comment
+// and TestEffectiveScaleCheckUsesReadyOnly, which asserts its generated
+// script never contains "2>/dev/null"). The fetch and the jq transform are
+// two separate statements (each with its own failure check) rather than one
+// piped line, matching this function's existing "capture first, check
+// status, THEN filter" idiom (ga-g7yt) — a piped `bd ... | jq ...` would
+// report jq's exit code on failure, masking a real bd failure exactly like
+// the pattern that doc comment warns against.
+func liveStepMoleculeIdsShell(quiet bool) string {
+	fetch := `live_step_molecules=$(bd list --status in_progress --type step --json --limit 0)`
+	transform := `live_step_molecules=$(printf "%s" "$live_step_molecules" | jq -c '[.[] | .parent | select(. != null)] | unique')`
+	if quiet {
+		return fetch + ` 2>/dev/null; ` +
+			transform + ` 2>/dev/null; ` +
+			`[ -z "$live_step_molecules" ] && live_step_molecules="[]"; `
+	}
+	return fetch + ` || exit $?; ` +
+		transform + ` || exit $?; ` +
+		`[ -z "$live_step_molecules" ] && live_step_molecules="[]"; `
+}
+
+// poolDemandExcludeLiveMoleculeStepJQ (ga-i5bu7) drops any candidate whose
+// mol-do-work molecule (metadata.molecule_id) currently has a live
+// (status=in_progress) step bead — i.e. the STORY bead was about to be
+// offered as fresh, unclaimed work to a brand-new worker while the
+// molecule's real state-carrying STEP bead was already in_progress under a
+// different, live worker. Root cause: the story stays open+unassigned for
+// the entire mol-do-work run (only the step tracks status), so nothing in
+// poolDemandLabelFilterJQ's label-based checks ever caught this — it needs
+// the story→molecule→step relational hop instead.
+//
+// Data model (verified against live bead JSON, both HQ graph.v2 step beads
+// and a closed whatsapp_automation mol-do-work story/molecule/step triple,
+// 2026-09-01): STORY.metadata.molecule_id -> MOLECULE.id; STEP.parent ==
+// MOLECULE.id, STEP.issue_type == "step". `bd list --parent <id>` (per `bd
+// list --help`) filters by exactly this parent edge.
+//
+// Reads $live_step_molecules, populated once per script by
+// liveStepMoleculeIdsShell — this stage itself never queries bd, so it
+// stays a pure, side-effect-free jq filter like poolDemandLabelFilterJQ and
+// can be piped immediately after it.
+//
+// A candidate with no molecule_id — the majority; most beads are not
+// mol-do-work roots — always survives: the `$mid == ""` branch short-
+// circuits before the live-set lookup, so this is a no-op for ordinary
+// beads and for every graph.v2 step-contract bead (those use
+// metadata.gc.root_bead_id, a different field, not metadata.molecule_id).
+func poolDemandExcludeLiveMoleculeStepJQ() string {
+	return `jq -c --argjson live_step_molecules "$live_step_molecules" ` + shellquote.Quote(
+		`[ .[] | select(((.metadata["molecule_id"] // "") as $mid | `+
+			`$mid == "" or (($live_step_molecules | index($mid)) == null))) ]`)
+}
